# API Conventions

## Error envelope (all endpoints)

```json
{
  "error": {
    "code": "QUOTE_NOT_FOUND",
    "message": "...",
    "correlation_id": "..."
  }
}
```

Pass through client `X-Correlation-Id` on errors when provided.

## Error codes

| Code | HTTP | When |
|------|------|------|
| `UNKNOWN_RATE_CARD` | 422 | Unknown cargo/vehicle combo |
| `QUOTE_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | No quote for shipment |
| `SNAPSHOT_NOT_FOUND` | 404 | No confirmed snapshot |
| `SNAPSHOT_ALREADY_EXISTS` | 409 | Second confirm on same shipment |
| `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT` | 409 | Same key, different shipment/context |

## Endpoints

- `POST .../shipments/{shipment_id}/quote` — create or return cached quote
- `GET .../shipments/{shipment_id}/quotes/latest`
- `POST .../shipments/{shipment_id}/confirm-snapshot` — requires `Idempotency-Key` header
- `GET .../shipments/{shipment_id}/snapshot`

## Idempotency (confirm-snapshot)

- No quote → 404
- Snapshot exists → 409 (even different idempotency key)
- Same key replay → 200, same snapshot, **no second event**
- Same key, different context → 409 `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`
- First success → 201, write snapshot, publish Redis event once
